  <content>
    <section>
      <para>
        
          <media alt="A graph. ">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_11_12_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <para> The graph above shows the population of a city from 1900 to 2000. Use the graph to answer questions 1 - 5.</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the average rate of change of the population between 1930 and 1950? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para/>
          <para>Compare your answers:</para>
          <para>About 250 people per year. The population was 40,000 in 1930 and about 45,000 in 1950, an increase of 5,000 people over 20 years, which equals 250 people per year.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
        <exercise id="a1675ebf-57d7-458b-b883-2c2253f7debe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1930 to 1940.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The correct answer is: positive.</para>
            <para>Try again. Work smarter, not harder! Take a moment to think about what you learned in the activity.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_86593013-6bb2-4b6c-b285-5c2d26f37ba4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1950 to 1970.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The correct answer is: negative.</para>
            <para>Try again. Work smarter, not harder! Take a moment to think about what you learned in the activity.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f5929df6-160f-4721-a943-5da6064a7541" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1930 to 1970.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The correct answer is: negative.</para>
            <para>Try again. Work smarter, not harder! Take a moment to think about what you learned in the activity.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>In which decade (10-year interval) did the population grow the fastest? Explain how you know.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para/>
          <para>Compare your answers:</para>
          <para>From 1910 to 1920. For example: The graph has the steepest slope between the two points on the graph \((1910,22)\) and \((1920,32)\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
